Photoplasm Licensing
Photoplasm follows a Pioreactor-style open-source model: core software is released under the MIT License, which permits broad reuse with required copyright and license attribution; documentation is licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0; and hardware designs are licensed under CERN-OHL-S v2. These licenses preserve attribution and, where applicable, reciprocal licensing requirements. The Photoplasm name, branding, proprietary know-how, unpublished processes, and separately protected inventions remain outside those blanket licenses.
/Software — MIT License
The MIT License applies to software and associated software documentation in this repository, unless a file explicitly states otherwise. It covers the /Software directory and any source code or script stored alongside other material (for example Docs/heater/*.py): placement does not change a file's license, its nature does.
